==Requirement Strategies==
*For the first and only requirement, since Boxten is one of the starter toons, you can just select him for free on the Start [[Toon]] Selection screen.
*If {{CI|Poppy|name=true}} was chosen instead, focus on picking up [[Research Capsules]] and extracting [[Machines]]. The Machine and Capsule count increase the further you descend, so you can earn more {{II|Ichor|name=true}}.

==Strategies==
Boxten's strength lies in Extraction. His [[Extraction Speed]] ranges from 1.06 to 1.594; this makes it above average ''at its lowest'' and 0.094 more than 5{{Star}} Extraction Speed at its highest, unless you are using Extraction Speed [[Trinkets]]. This makes him a good choice to earn {{TI|Ichor|name=true}} through [[Machines]] when starting out. However, since he is heavily dependent on teammates for maximum Extraction Speed, if you prefer playing with a small team (1-4 players), other [[Toons]] such as {{CI|Glisten|name=true}}, {{CI|Yatta|name=true}}, or {{CI|Vee|name=true}} will be better suited in this occasion. His [[Ability]], '''Wind-Up''', allows access to over 5 Star Extraction Speed, but since these Stats are obtainable without using the Ability slot (which is a source of bonus Ichor), it's similar to playing without any Ability at all. Worse than that is the fact that his Ability relies on factors out of your control, which makes Boxten outclassed by a lot of Toons.

Assuming you're in a team with enough players (around 5-8), you can be a very efficient stealthy extractor, especially if there's a distractor with 2 or 3 Star [[Stealth]]. Using {{TI|Diary|name=true}} furthers this by allowing you to extract near 3 Star Stealth teammates with little to no risk involving [[Twisteds]]. This all could make him more viable than low Stealth, high Extraction Speed Toons such as Glisten, {{CI|Squirm|name=true}}, and Yatta, due to the ability to extract quickly near a variety of distractors.

Generally, it's recommended to use Boxten in games with a lot of Toons to get the most value out of his Ability. Though, he is quite iffy for solo runs, due to his Ability relying solely on other teammates, wasting it. He is a great option for long runs however, because if his teammates can stay alive, it gives him quite a bit more than 5 Star Extraction Speed, with decent Stats across the others.

Boxten benefits from being on a team with Toons that can boost his Extraction Speed, such as {{CI|Brusha|name=true}}, {{CI|Shelly|name=true}}, or {{CI|Cocoa|name=true}}. The boosts multiply with Boxten's passive, creating a particularly potent stacked increase that could allow him to fill Machines in no time, while also getting more use out of the boosts, minimizing potential wastage.

He can benefit from survival [[Items]], helping his average [[Movement Speed]], which can make escape from Twisteds tedious, especially for newer players. [[Stamina]] items can help remedy poor Stamina management or improve his mobility. Extraction Speed or Skill Check increasing items can further improve his variably decent-phenomenal extraction. This is especially the case for percentage based Extraction Speed boosts from Items such as {{II|Extraction Speed Candy|name=false}} or {{II|Instructions|name=false}}, as their boosts will multiply with Wind Up's boost.

His average Stat spread means that while he has no true deficits, he also doesn't have the most potent strengths. Supplementing your personal weaknesses with Trinkets is best while using him. Using Trinkets that stack with his Extraction Speed can also work, such as {{TI|Stress Ball|name=true}} (where he can reach upwards of 83.3% as a boost with 8 living players).

Overall, Boxten is a pretty good starter Toon, but can sometimes be outclassed by other Toons with better Extraction, except possibly those with lower Stealth.

