==Trivia==
*At the end of the [[Boxten/Gallery#Development|Meet Boxten Teaser Video]], morse code can be heard that translates to "FIND THE {{Tape}}[[Tapes|TAPES]]."
**This is also one of the texts that can appear when starting a new run {{Small|(at the bottom of the elevator screen)}}.
*Boxten's name could originate from a combination of the name "Boston" and "Box", though it could be a play on the phrase "Boxed In" as well.
*Boxten loves trivia, according to his interaction with {{CI|Vee|name=true}}.
*Boxten worries a lot, which is pointed out by {{CI|Poppy|name=true}} in one of their interactions, his interaction with {{CI|Rodger|name=true}}, and some of his dialogue.
**{{CI|Cosmo|name=true}} and {{CI|Teagan|name=true}}'s interactions with him might also be considered as hinting at Boxten worrying a lot.
*Though Boxten and [[Poppy]] seem to be good friends, [[Qwel]] has said that they have no confirmed relations.
**They share a lot of similarities.
***Most (if not all) of their similarities are due to them being the starters [[Toons]] of the game.
****Whoever isn't chosen as the player's first Toon costs 100 {{TI|Ichor|name=true}}, therefore, they both have no other requirements except for a certain amount of Ichor.
*****The Price use to be 250 Ichor each before being reduced at an unknown time.
***They both have 3{{Star}} on all of their [[Stats]] and share the same Stat spread with all of the {{Type|Common}} [[Event Toons]].
****However, since Boxten's [[Ability]] affects himself as well, it always allows him to have at least slightly higher Extraction Speed than them.
****{{CI|Razzle & Dazzle|name=true}} could also count if not considering their Abilities.
***Both their [[Twisted]] counterparts are {{Type|Common}}, have average stats, and no mechanic to aid them.
***They both have an official [[merchandise]] plush.
****They are the only non-{{Type|Rare}}, non-{{Type|Main}}, and non-{{Type|Lethal}} Toons to have so.
***Both their respective [[Trinkets]], respectively {{TI|Blue Bandana|name=true}} and {{TI|Pink Bow|name=true}}, are present in their models and have mechanics that resemble their Abilities.
***They have 4 [[Mastery]] quests in common, being "Survive 25 [[Floors]]!", "Travel 50000 Meters!", "Pick 30 [[Items]]!", and "Use 30 Items!".
****For their other quests, Boxten needs to finish 20 more [[Machines]] than Poppy does, and Poppy needs to activate her Ability 30 times, while Boxten needs to survive a Floor with all 8 players alive (which also reflects his Ability, since it's where he would get to his full potential).
***They both have [[Skins]] whose skin color doesn't change, being {{Skin|Creepy Chord}} and {{Skin|Sapphire Dots}} respectively.
***Their [[Christmas]] Skins, respectively {{Skin|Quiet Caroler}} and {{Skin|Confident Caroler}}, are probably meant to match for being both "carolers".
***They both have 2 interactions with {{CI|Looey|name=true}}.
***They got optimized in the same [[update]], along with [[Cosmo]], {{CI|Sprout|name=true}}, and {{CI|Dandy|name=true}}.
***When bought in [[Dandy's Store]], Dandy says "{{Text|_ is a great choice!}}" for both of them.
***They both have "Meet _" teaser videos with morse code at the end of each one.
***They were one of the first Toons to get [[merchandise]] plushes after the [[Main Characters]].
*Boxten might not be very good with grammar, as seen on the note in Boxten's room in [[Roleplay Mode]].
*The key on the back of Boxten's head turns when he's focused, as shown in his former and current extracting animation, and in his interactions with [[Cosmo]] and {{CI|Ginger|name=true}}.
**Boxten's key also spins almost rapidly while running as seen in his {{CI|Twisted Boxten}}[[Twisted Boxten|Twisted counterpart]], likely alluding to this as well.
*Boxten, at a very early point in the game {{Small|(about one week after the public release)}}, would only receive a 5% [[Extraction Speed]] boost per alive [[Toon]], maxing at 40% or 1.40 units.
*According to [[Cosmo]]'s interaction with Boxten, he has a bit of knowledge with baking.
**This is further proven in one of [[Sprout]]'s interactions with [[Shelly]], saying that Cosmo is teaching Boxten how to bake.
*Other [[Toons]] tend to notice Boxten's square head, as shown in his interactions with {{CI|Goob|name=true}} and [[Looey]].
*Boxten, along with [[Looey]], are the only [[Toons]] that can roughly reach 17 Stars in their [[Stat]] pool without any [[Cards]] or [[Items]]. Boxten is ahead by 0.094% in Extraction Speed and Looey is behind by 6.67% in Walk Speed and 20% in Run Speed (Looey gains 20% Movement Speed for every {{Heart}} missing).
*Boxten, [[Poppy]], and [[Cosmo]] are the first Common [[Toons]] that weren't previously optimized to receive an optimized model.
*Boxten can't entirely understand {{CI|Flutter|name=true}}, having stated such himself in an interaction with her.
**Despite this, he is still shown to be decent at it in this interaction and his other interaction with Flutter, where he asks how she's doing, and ends apologizing after her response. In the latter example, however, it's possible he was just going off of her tone and her obviously being upset.
**As Boxten can play music (as confirmed in [[Dandy]]'s [[gossip]] about him and implied in his interaction with {{CI|Shrimpo|name=true}}) and Flutter's wings are implied to be loud (in one of her interactions with Shrimpo), this could contribute to Boxten not hearing her very well, due to him hearing his music and Flutter's wings at the same time, though this is just speculation.
*Boxten is the only [[Toon]] to not have his base [[Extraction Speed]] units be in one decimal place, with his usually being in two unless 4 other Toons are with him.
*If not counting his {{Skin|Vintage}} [[Skin]], {{Skin|Quiet Caroler}} is the first and only Boxten Skin whose skin color is not a shade of purple, being a dark red instead.
*Boxten is the first [[Toon]] whose head can open up, with the second being {{CI|Gigi|name=true}}.
**Their [[Twisted]] counterparts both have [[Ichor]] hands going through those parts.
*Since [[Changelog|v0.15.17]], while Boxten's Passive [[Ability]] says it caps at 48%, it actually caps at 59.4% in game. This is due to his Ability now adding to the Extraction Speed Multiplier rather than his base Extraction Speed directly. The reason for this was to make his Ability match its description more accurately, though its description hasn't been changed.
*Due to his [[Ability]], Boxten has the potential to have the highest consistent [[Extraction Speed]]. This is done by playing with 7 other players, using both [[Blue Bandana]] & {{TI|Lucky Coin|name=true}}, and getting a [[Dandy]] mask from either a [[Haunted Gala]] or the "Dandy Mask!" Treat from [[Trick or Treat Doors]]. His Extraction Speed will be almost 2.88 (≈18 seconds).
**He will also extract faster if {{CDI|Tech Savvy|name=true}} is chosen, though only because it decreases the amount of units a [[Machine]] needs to be completed by 5 units, rather than directly affecting Extraction Speed.
*In the starter [[Toon]] menu added in [[Changelog|v0.22.1]], Boxten's face is comprised of multiple 3D assets for his eyes and mouth instead of 2D textures. This was likely to make the facial expressions easier to do without tons of textures being needed.
*Boxten acts as the representative [[Toon]] for the "Toons" option in the highlight accessibility settings. He mirrors this trait with his [[Twisted Boxten|Twisted counterpart]], who is the representative [[Twisted]] for an analogous option.

